{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/211964-so-the-apocalypse","id":211964,"title":"So the apocalypse...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-28T19:58:56-07:00","id":211964,"title":"So the apocalypse...","content":"Do the werewolves have the worst of it? I imagine that the other fallen world scenarios occur before the wyrm apocalypse yes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:42:46-07:00","id":212006,"title":"","content":"No. In the Ascension scenario &quot;Hell On Earth&quot; things pretty much suck more than in any other. After all, in none of the Werewolf Apocalypse scenarios do the bad guys win such a shut out victory as to TURN OVER CREATION ITSELF to the Nephandi and their masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T11:43:09-07:00","id":212642,"title":"","content":"Yeah <i>Hell on Earth</i> is about the worst of the big three lines. It's been a long time since I've read <i>Time of Judgment </i>so I don't remember about their scenarios though I was greatly disappoint with much of that book simply because they crammed the ends of five different lines into a single book, forcing them to skim on all of them.<br /> <br /> Of course WtO's grand finale, <i>Ends of Empire</i>, was quite destructive and apocalyptic it was just limited to the Underworld. And Orpheus's end saw the players confronting Grandmother, one of the most powerful, if not <i>the </i>most powerful, entities/forces we've seen in the CWoD and is bent on consuming the Underworld, Earth, <i>everything</i>. In fact the name Grandmother is a mistake. The spectres that she controls refer to her as 'the Grand Maw' which non-spectres have mistaken for Grandma, hence the name. So failing to stop her would result in the eventual end of everything which would be much worse than the <i>Hell on Earth </i>scenario. Though I should also note that Grandmother isn't actually evil, she doesn't comprehend the nature of life and the universe outside the spectre hive mind and is consuming the universe so that she can use all that energy to create the universe. So after everything was destroyed something new would come into existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T16:14:46-07:00","id":212898,"title":"","content":"is that what she is? Because she's mentioned in one of the werewolf end time scenarios.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T16:25:04-07:00","id":212910,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, the Kindred of the East ending wasn't all that much fun; Mikaboshi becomes the Demon Emperor, turns the earth into hell, and everyone suffers horrifically forever and ever.<br /> <br /> And you had that one Vampire scenario where Tzimisci assimilates everything in the entire world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T18:11:12-07:00","id":213002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/211964-so-the-apocalypse?p=212898#post212898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is that what she is? Because she's mentioned in one of the werewolf end time scenarios.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I believe that's the Weaver and the Wyrm restored back to what they were before they fell out of balance.<br /> <br /> As for Grandmother they never really explain what she is. We know she's tied to the spectres and Oblivion, she's a part of the hive mind and the Neverborn came from her. The two most common ideas is that she's either the personification of Oblivion awakened by the Sixth Great Maelstrom or God's/the Creator's dark half/twin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T07:20:01-07:00","id":213524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/211964-so-the-apocalypse?p=213002#post213002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I believe that's the Weaver and the Wyrm restored back to what they were before they fell out of balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, not the cheesy end speech of Weaver Ascendant. It's in A Tribe Falls, for the Silent Striders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T10:33:48-07:00","id":213706,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Haven't read the book in ages and it was my second least favorite of the endline books. And that's the first time I've ever seen Orpheus material referenced outside of Orpheus. Kind of strange consider Orpheus has always been treated as the little kid in the back corner of class that everyone ignores and tries to forget about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T13:50:42-07:00","id":213949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/211964-so-the-apocalypse?p=212910#post212910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, the Kindred of the East ending wasn't all that much fun; Mikaboshi becomes the Demon Emperor, turns the earth into hell, and everyone suffers horrifically forever and ever.<br /> <br /> And you had that one Vampire scenario where Tzimisci assimilates everything in the entire world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but doesn't the Demon Emperor HAVE to come and rule over the Sixth Age in order for the Wheel to turn back to the next one? And don't the players ultimately destroy Tzimisce and restore the world to normal? ''Hell on Earth'' has the bad guy <i>win</i>, no backsies or Saulot-ex-machina or eternal cosmic cycle. The Nephandi take over the universe, full stop, and darkness rules forevermore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T16:42:58-07:00","id":214018,"title":"","content":"Yeah in theory the Sixth Age will eventually end, leading to a pretty crappy but better Age which in turn will lead to a better Age until it gets back to the golden First Age before descending down to another Sixth Age.<br /> <br /> Of course the same could be said for Ascension's <i>Hell on Earth</i> scenario as it points out at the end of that chapter that while the world as we know it ends the world <i>itself </i>does not and even makes some comments that sound an awful lot like the Wheel of Ages and how it always turns. Of course it also comments that it would be a great uphill battle for the survivors among the Traditions, Conventions and Crafts but like with the rest of MtAs anything and everything is possible, even the most impossible of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}